==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|la|[[dēlīrium]] [[tremēns]]|lit=trembling madness}}, {{coin|en|Thomas Sutton|w=Thomas Sutton (physician)|in=1813|nobycat=1|nocap=1}}.<ref>{{cite-book|author=Thomas Sutton|authorlink=Thomas Sutton (physician)|title=Tracts on Delirium Tremens, &c.|year=1813|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/tractsondelirium00sutt/page/3/mode/1up|location=London|page=3|passage=The name, therefore, which I have adopted, though possibly not the most appropriate, will serve to convey a notion of an essential symptom of the disease, and will be sufficiently explicit for my present purpose.}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|nolinkhead=1}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A [[psychosis]] of chronic [[alcoholism]], usually due to [[alcohol]] withdrawal, which can be fatal. Symptoms include sweating, tremors, terrifying [[hallucination]]s, [[insomnia]], restlessness, [[disorientation]] and anxiety.
#: {{syn|en|DT|phrenitis|q2=obsolete}}

